All six features are implemented and verified. Here's what changed:

**`app/auth.py`** — `require_api_key` now reads the `X-API-Key` header, validates it against `VALID_API_KEYS`, and raises `HTTPException(401)` when missing or invalid. It returns the associated username on success.

**`app/main.py`** — Added four new endpoints and upgraded `GET /tasks`:

- `GET /tasks` now accepts optional query params `status`, `priority`, `assigned_to` (combinable), and `page`/`page_size` (defaults 1 and 20).
- `POST /tasks` requires auth, validates `project_id` (404 if missing), auto-generates the next integer ID, and returns the created task with status 201.
- `PUT /tasks/{task_id}` requires auth, supports partial updates via `TaskUpdate`, and returns 404 if the task doesn't exist.
- `DELETE /tasks/{task_id}` requires auth, removes the task, and returns 204 on success or 404 if not found.

FastAPI imports cleanly and a live test run confirmed auth rejection, filtering, pagination, create/update/delete, and combined filters all behave correctly.
